# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keep your hub's own records out of commits (added in 1.38.0)
#
# After Kick-off, a clone of this repository works as your DSM hub.
# Your sessions then write lessons, memory, worklogs and messages from
# your spoke projects into it. Those records describe your work, not
# the methodology, and a fork of a public repository on GitHub is
# public as well, so they are never committed.
#
# Claude Code normally hides .claude/ through .git/info/exclude. The
# .claude/ lines below still apply when that exclude is missing.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Messages from your spoke projects stay local; the README that
# explains the folder is kept.
_inbox/*
!_inbox/README.md

# Lessons the hub collects from its spokes.
dsm-docs/reasoning-lessons-ecosystem.md

# Working records of your agent sessions.
.claude/worklog.md
.claude/memory/
.claude/reasoning-lessons-compact.md
.claude/last-staa.txt

# Lesson-sharing record and private scan terms.
.claude/lessons-shared.txt
.claude/leak-scan-patterns.txt
